    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9088" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">collīsĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conl-</span></b> ),
		ōnis, f.
		collido, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a dashing</i> or <i>striking
			together</i>, <i>a concussion</i>, <i>shock</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">partūs abjecti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Just. 11, 12, 6</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of letters in a word: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πνεῖν, χεἰν, ῥεῖν</span>, non sunt integra,
			sed ex collisione contracta. <i><span class="en">Macr. Diff. 19,
				§ 17</span></i>.</div>
